# Esc during a running /compact cancels it (internal/tui/app.go: Esc with
# m.background set cancels its context) instead of waiting for it to
# finish or hanging: the note names the command's own CancelNote
# ("Compaction cancelled. The conversation is as it was."), and the
# conversation is left exactly as it was, not half-compacted.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/hooks-esc-during-compaction.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE turn one
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Sure, working on it\./ 20
TYPE turn two
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Second turn done\./ 20
TYPE /compact
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Compacting conversation/ 10
SHOT compacting
KEY esc
WAITFOR /Compaction cancelled\. The conversation is as it was\./ 10
SHOT cancelled
EXPECT /Compaction cancelled\. The conversation is as it was\./
EXPECT_NOT /Context compacted/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
